# Template for .env — copy, then fill in real values:
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#   $EDITOR .env
#   set -a && source .env && set +a
#
# .env is gitignored and must never be committed. This file is the only one of
# the pair that is tracked, so it must contain PLACEHOLDERS ONLY — never a real
# key. The daemon reads plain environment variables; it does not parse .env
# itself.

# ---- Direct mode (your own provider key goes straight to the provider) ----

# Base URL of an OpenAI-compatible API. Required — the daemon refuses to start
# without it.
MOCHIII_API_BASE=https://openrouter.ai/api/v1

# Sent as "Authorization: Bearer <key>". May be left empty for local
# OpenAI-compatible servers that don't require one.
MOCHIII_API_KEY=sk-or-v1-xxxxx

# ---- Proxy mode (the managed pilot path; see ./run-proxy.sh) --------------

# Your per-user Mochiii key, used to authenticate to the managed proxy. The
# proxy holds the OpenRouter key server-side, so in proxy mode this is the ONLY
# credential on your machine — leave MOCHIII_API_KEY unset there.
MOCHIII_PROXY_KEY=mochi_xxxxx

# Set by ./run-proxy.sh; you don't normally set it here. When "true", the daemon
# authenticates with MOCHIII_PROXY_KEY instead of MOCHIII_API_KEY
# and expects MOCHIII_API_BASE to point at the proxy. It is the switch that
# selects proxy mode, not a label: unset, the daemon stays in direct mode.
# MOCHIII_USE_PROXY=true

# The proxy MOCHIII_API_BASE must point at in proxy mode. ./run-proxy.sh
# sets this for you and ignores the direct-mode value above, so it is recorded
# here only so the URL is discoverable — uncommenting it would break direct
# mode. Not a secret: a public HTTPS endpoint that refuses unauthenticated
# requests.
# MOCHIII_API_BASE=https://codeterminal-core-production.up.railway.app/v1

# Points ./run-proxy.sh at a DIFFERENT proxy (e.g. a local one under test).
# This is the only way to do that: the script never takes the proxy URL from
# MOCHIII_API_BASE, so a direct-mode setting can't decide where a Mochiii
# key is sent.
# MOCHIII_PROXY_BASE=http://localhost:8080/v1
